<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Odysseus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ulysses</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Odysseus, called Ulysses by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, is the legendary king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ithaca">Ithaca</a> in Greek myth, a hero of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trojan-war">Trojan War</a> famous for his cunning, credited with the stratagem of the wooden horse. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odyssey">Odyssey</a> tells of his ten-year voyage home, including his escape from the Cyclops Polyphemus. Many Greek and Italian cities claimed him or his sons as founders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/odysseus.jpg" alt="Odysseus" width="320" height="378" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jastrow · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Head_Odysseus_MAR_Sperlonga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
